Make -P (plain connection, no TLS) work, and report why connecting failed.

Since upstream commit d0d9ed5 redir_connect creates a connection context only
for TLS, so with -P amtterm, amtider and gamt close every connection.  This is
upstream merge request !3, not yet merged:
https://gitlab.com/kraxel/amtterm/-/merge_requests/3

From 5b79b25a7933ee4b770b892393f695d31cdaa44d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam Curtis <adam.curtis.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 17:45:27 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] redir: set the connect error message before reporting it

Set r->err before redir_connect() switches to REDIR_ERROR.

Fixes blank error messages on failed connection.

Signed-off-by: Adam Curtis <adam.curtis.dev@gmail.com>
---
 redir.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/redir.c b/redir.c
index 70d6100..4b2d24e 100644
--- a/redir.c
+++ b/redir.c
@@ -167,9 +167,9 @@ int redir_connect(struct redir *r)
 	r->sock = -1;
     }
     if (-1 == r->sock) {
-	redir_state(r, REDIR_ERROR);
 	/* FIXME: better error message */
 	snprintf(r->err, sizeof(r->err), "connect failed");
+	redir_state(r, REDIR_ERROR);
 	return -1;
     }
     return 0;
-- 
